// ⚠ `cliff` LEFT — plan 22 `B1c.2a`. Its own header named `hex_edge`'s shared
// layer as its target home and said it sat here only because moving to another
// agent's tree is an ask; `hex_editor` is the waypoint, because that is where the
// WALKER is going and *the rule about what a walker can climb belongs with the
// walker*. `stair_cut` in `hex_editor` carried the mirror of that note — "it came
// from `moros_sim::stair_height`, a MOROS package, and this is a lavition one, so
// taking the dependency would point the arrow backwards" — and this is that debt
// paid rather than routed around. Nothing in this package's `src/` ever called it.
// ⚠ `fall` LEFT FOR `hex_editor` — plan 22 `B1c.3`. The editor's walker lives there
// now and a walker that cannot fall is half of one; this package could not be
// depended on from a lavition one. ⚠ Its constants were IMPORTED from `player` under
// *"a package with two gravities is a package where a jump and a fall disagree"* —
// still true, and no longer the same package: `player_step` falls in a `Map`, that
// one falls in a `VoxelWorld`, and each pins its own value with a test naming the
// other. Nothing in this package's `src/` ever called it.
